                  <provenance type="#l"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_190">Ely, Cambridgeshire.
                        Benedictine abbey and (1109) cathedral priory of St Peter and St Etheldreda</orgName><p>J.B.L. Tolhurst comments in a letter to N.R. Ker 13 July 1943
                        "The mention of pontifex in a rubric in col. 2 and the Ely saints in the
                        litany point unmistakably to that Cathedral Priory". The other leaf now in
                        XVIII.B.2.13, from the same source appears to be from a different service
                        book. </p></provenance>
